CASE: a log the analyser could not parse
The steering arm's log has no join line and no round in it at all. THIS IS THE
CASE THE FIRST CUT OF THE GUARD COULD NOT CATCH: it read
`if joins and len(joins) > 1`, which is satisfied by an EMPTY list -- and an
empty list is exactly the symptom of the parsing bug the guard exists to
survive (the join regex had been anchored on `[0]` while the server decorates a
join with the joining client's own id). A guard satisfied by having found
nothing is not a guard. It now requires EXACTLY ONE join per arm.

